  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/peckoltia-wernekei",
      "html": "<p><em>Peckoltia wernekei</em>, also known as L243 and LDA086, is a suckermouth catfish known only from parts of the upper Río Orinoco drainage in Amazonas state, southern Venezuela. Armbruster and Lujan described it in 2016 from the Ventuari drainage. It is sometimes confused with <em>Peckoltia lineola</em>, alongside which it is often exported for the aquarium trade.</p>"
    },
